# Engine

3D does three things here and no more:
it holds the page plane, it gives the camera something to look at, and it writes depth for the lens.
The interface itself stays in canvas 2D, in the shots and the kit.

## Decisions that cost time

- The page canvas is uploaded as plain RGBA8:
  `NoColorSpace`, `flipY = false`, `premultiplyAlpha = true`, and the sRGB decode happens in the shader.
  An sRGB texture with `flipY` takes the CPU path in Chrome and costs seconds per 4K frame.
  These settings in `page.ts` do not change.
- The master has no MSAA (`QUALITY.master.msaa` is 0) and uses FXAA.
  Multisampling a half-float target at 4K was about twenty times slower.
- Page density is 1.5× in draft, 2.5× in high and 5× in master,
  so type stays sharp when a 4K frame looks at a third of the page.
- The video frame is read in the task that drew it.
  The drawing buffer is valid only then.
- A stage is timed with a one-pixel `readPixels` fence, never with `gl.finish()`:
  Chrome turns `finish()` into a flush.
  `pipe.timings` does this.
- Every effect scales with the frame height,
  so a 1080p preview and the 4K master frame the same picture.
  A new effect follows this rule.
- three.js and mp4-muxer are pinned to exact versions in `package.json`.
  An upgrade is a commit of its own, with frames compared before and after and with timings.

## Contracts that other code relies on

- `window.__film` (`FilmApi` in `player.ts`) is what the tools call.
  A change to a member changes `tools/`, the skill's `references/shot-api.md`
  and `docs/en/pipeline.md` in the same commit.
- `edit.stateAt(t)` is pure — [determinism](determinism.mdc).
- `exportMP4` stays deterministic:
  frame `i` is time `i / fps`, with no screen capture and no dropped frames.
- The shaders live in `shaders.ts` as template strings.
  The tone map follows the Khronos PBR Neutral reference and keeps its credit in `NOTICE.md`.

## Changing the engine

- Compare frames before and after — [verification](verification.mdc) —
  and record `bun run timings` when a pass changed.
- A new option enters `makeEdit` with a default that leaves the current look as it is.
